Klethron tsnet modifies two tailscale.com source files in an isolated build copy.
Upstream revision: 5b6c39b94d50beac39dd7302d6f75f14e281a01f
Original file SHA-256:
control/controlclient/direct.go: a28e97e2a6822604182cdcfdd319ea9bb10c29b17e8b4592289c1cf2278160a9
tsnet/dns_lookup.go: b49ecd66f1b9f4de7e7ef20061148a0e903de2e847627db38c88715c6964dc93

The build verifies upstream modules and rejects changes to these source files.
The shared Go module cache remains unchanged. A temporary go.mod replaces
tailscale.com with ./tailscale; binary build metadata records that replacement.
The inventory's Tailscale checksum identifies the upstream module before these
patches, not the modified copy. BuildGoLibrary.kt applies these changes:

--- a/control/controlclient/direct.go
+++ b/control/controlclient/direct.go
@@ -513,3 +513,5 @@
-	c.mu.Lock()
-	c.persist = new(persist.Persist).View()
-	c.mu.Unlock()
+	if err == nil {
+		c.mu.Lock()
+		c.persist = new(persist.Persist).View()
+		c.mu.Unlock()
+	}

TryLogout forgets the node key only when control confirmed the logout. Upstream
also forgets it after a failed request; the map poll continues and saves the
empty key over the stored login, leaving the node registered at control with no
local key with which to log out again.

--- a/tsnet/dns_lookup.go
+++ b/tsnet/dns_lookup.go
@@ -218 +218 @@
-		return c.hostLookup(ctx, network, hostFB)
+		return candidateResult{servfail: true, err: firstErr}

A name that no tailnet DNS route covers, and whose tailnet queries all fail,
counts as a failed lookup. Upstream then asks the host's resolver, which sends
the name to the device's network and lets that network's DNS answer with any
address, including a reachable tailnet address.
